From: TNG Technical Manual compatibility investigation
Subject: [PATCH] DIRECTOR: Trace Trek Tech resume-page variable scopes

The attempted resume fix proved that the movie-global gPLData exists, but a
Ready Room quit still stores the stale ship-exterior page. Before making any
further behavioral change, record both Director's normal variable resolution
and explicit global resolution at the exact shutdown getAt(gPLData, 1) call.

Also dump the variables visible in that handler so the authoritative current
page can be identified from one controlled quit test. This patch is diagnostic
only: the GLOBALREF behavior introduced by the preceding compatibility patch
is left unchanged.
---
 engines/director/lingo/lingo-bytecode.cpp | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/engines/director/lingo/lingo-bytecode.cpp b/engines/director/lingo/lingo-bytecode.cpp
index 05d83d22..132b25ad 100644
--- a/engines/director/lingo/lingo-bytecode.cpp
+++ b/engines/director/lingo/lingo-bytecode.cpp
@@ -457,6 +457,18 @@ void LC::cb_objectcall() {
 				g_lingo->_state->context && g_lingo->_state->context->_id == 193 &&
 				var.u.s->equalsIgnoreCase("getAt") &&
 				firstArg.u.s->equalsIgnoreCase("gPLData")) {
+			Datum normalRef = firstArg;
+			normalRef.type = VARREF;
+			Datum globalRef = firstArg;
+			globalRef.type = GLOBALREF;
+			Datum normalValue = g_lingo->varFetch(normalRef, true);
+			Datum globalValue = g_lingo->varFetch(globalRef, true);
+			warning("TNG RESUME DIAGNOSTIC: normal gPLData [%s] %s",
+					normalValue.type2str(), normalValue.asString(true).c_str());
+			warning("TNG RESUME DIAGNOSTIC: global gPLData [%s] %s",
+					globalValue.type2str(), globalValue.asString(true).c_str());
+			warning("TNG RESUME DIAGNOSTIC VARIABLES:\n%s",
+					g_lingo->formatAllVars().c_str());
 			// Score script 193 omits its global declaration, but Director 4
 			// resolves this legacy reference to the movie's playlist global.
 			firstArg.type = GLOBALREF;
